# Test some basic functionality of kit-mdc when operating on object files.
#
# Create temporary working directories
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: rm -rf %t/in && mkdir -p %t/in
#
# Create the object files to be used for testing. The sources are checked in
# to avoid having binary blobs checked in. We need an object file created from
# an empty input file.
#
# RUN: llc -o %t/in/empty.o -filetype=obj %S/input/empty.ll
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If the input object does not contain any embedded device code, an output
# file should not be created
#
# RUN: kit-mdc -o %t/empty-extracted.o %t/in/empty.o
# RUN: not cat %t/empty-extracted.o
